 2. GitHub repo létrehozása (iPhone Safariból)


1. github.com → New repo: "my-ios-app"
2. Add .github/workflows/ios-build.yml:


iosbuild.yml (copypaste):
yaml
name: iOS Build
on: [workflow_dispatch, repository_dispatch]
jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: macos-14
    steps:
    - uses: actions/checkout@v4

    - name: Setup Xcode
      uses: maxim-lobanov/setup-xcode@v1
      with:
        xcode-version: latest-stable

    - name: Build IPA
      run: |
        swift build
        xcodebuild -scheme MyApp -sdk iphoneos -configuration Release archive -archivePath ./build/MyApp.xcarchive CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Automatic
        xcodebuild -exportArchive -archivePath ./build/MyApp.xcarchive -exportPath ./build -exportOptionsPlist exportOptions.json

    - name: Upload IPA
      uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
      with:
        name: MyApp.ipa
        path: build/MyApp.ipa


exportOptions.json:
json
{
  "method": "development",
  "teamID": "YOUR_TEAM_ID"
}


 3. iPhoneon a teljes flow (3 perc)


1. Replit shell: npm run build-ios
   ↓ (GitHub Actions elindul macOS runner-en)

2. GitHub → Actions → kattints az IPA artifact-ra → Download

3. iPhone Files app → IPA bemásolása → dupla tap → Install


